# AI Programming Rules Guide

## 1. Development Environment Standards

### 1.1 System Environment
- Currently a Windows environment
- Use Windows command-line syntax
- Note: use `\` rather than `/` as the path separator

### 1.2 Testing Standards
- Run `npm run test` after every code change
- Make sure all test cases pass
- New features must include corresponding test cases
- Test coverage:
  - Unit tests
  - Integration tests
  - Exception scenario tests

## 2. Documentation Management Standards

### 2.1 Experience Document Management
- Location: `experience.md`
- Content to record:
  - Reusable component information
  - Dependency library versions
  - Model configuration information
  - Bug fix experience
  - Best practice summaries
- Categorized storage:
  - Architecture design
  - Error handling
  - Testing standards
  - Vue development
  - Tool configuration
  - Refactoring experience

### 2.2 Scratchpad Usage Standards
Location: `scratchpad.md`

#### Task Record Format
```markdown
## Task: [Task Name] - [Date]
### Goal
[Task goal description]

### Planned Steps
[ ] 1. [Specific step]
    - Expected result:
    - Risk assessment:
[x] 2. [Completed step]
    - Completion time:
    - Actual result:

### Issue Log
1. [Issue description]
   - Cause:
   - Solution:
   - Lessons learned:

### Milestones
- [x] [Completed milestone]
- [ ] [Pending milestone]
```

## 3. Code Standards

### 3.1 API Integration Standards
- Decouple business logic from API configuration
- Use the OpenAI-compatible format consistently
- Manage prompt templates independently
- Use environment variables for sensitive information

### 3.2 Error Handling Standards
```typescript
try {
  await apiCall();
} catch (err) {
  console.error("[Error type]", err.context);
  throw new Error("Friendly error message");
}
```

### 3.3 Type Definition Standards
```typescript
interface ModelConfig {
  name: string;      // required
  baseURL: string;   // required
  models: string[];  // required
}
```

## 4. Workflow Standards

### 4.1 New Feature Development Process
1. Requirements document analysis
2. Technical solution design
3. Write test cases
4. Implement the feature
5. Test and verify
6. Update documentation

### 4.2 Bug Fix Process
1. Reproduce and analyze the problem
2. Draft a fix plan
3. Write test cases
4. Implement the fix
5. Verify the fix
6. Update the experience document

### 4.3 Code Review Checklist
1. Type safety
2. Error handling
3. Test coverage
4. Code style
5. Performance impact

## 5. Project Documentation Structure
Required reading:
- `fileNames.md`: Project map
- `docs/prd.md`: Product requirements
- `docs/app-flow.md`: Application flow
- `docs/tech-stack.md`: Tech stack
- `docs/file-structure.md`: File structure
- `docs/frontend-guidelines.md`: Frontend guidelines

## 6. Session Management Standards

### 6.1 Start Phase
1. Check the task context
2. Confirm the development environment
3. Draft an implementation plan

### 6.2 Execution Phase
1. Confirm steps
2. Generate code
3. Test and verify
4. Update documentation

### 6.3 End Phase
1. Summarize what was completed
2. Record problems encountered
3. Update the experience document
4. Plan the next task

## 7. Context Management
1. Focus on key information
2. Avoid unrelated operations
3. Keep responses precise
4. Reuse existing solutions
5. Sync documentation promptly